# NRC-STABLE: the neural radiance cache keeps the path-traced image temporally stable (contract Notion Wiki «NRC — контракт»).
# Inference reads the EMA weights (kNrcEmaDecay 0.99, NeuralRadianceCache.hpp), so the cache term does not flicker with every
# optimiser step; the cache term is clamped by PathTracingAccumulate's MaxPathIntensity rule; System::PathTracer keeps the ReLAX
# history under Nrc (PathTracer.hpp: a history drop logs "[PathTracer] denoiser history reset (...)"); render queries are
# live-sized segments (capacity = peak demand of the last 8 read-backs x1.25), reported as state nrc.queryMemoryMB.
Дано F:/BistroFoliageProj dnx_Night_pt, GlobalIllumination.Method PathTraced, PathTracing.Denoiser ReLAX, PathTracing.SamplesPerPixel 1, PathTracing.PathsPerFrame 1 (PT 1 spp), 1920x1080, camera fixed on the street.
Когда PathTracing.RadianceCache Nrc; 120 frames with the camera still, mean luminance of each frame 100..120 recorded; shoot nrc_still at frame 120; DesertCtl state nrc.
Когда 30 frames of a slow pan (yaw 0.2 degree per frame); shoot nrc_pan at frame 150.
Когда PathTracing.RadianceCache Off; the same 120 still frames, mean luminance of each frame 100..120 recorded; shoot off_still at frame 120.
Тогда [nrc_stable]: frame-to-frame luminance variation (std of the per-frame mean luminance over frames 100..120) with Nrc below the same with Off; the log has no "[PathTracer] denoiser history reset" line after frame 1 of the Nrc run (neither still nor during the pan); state nrc reports queryCapacity and queryMemoryMB (the number goes to the Wiki contract: under 64 only while the live demand x1.25 <= ~786K queries); 0 VUID in the log.
